    "summary": "gh-1679 [GOAL] Provider-key persistence must be loud: wizard save failures surface on the spot (kimi_ira 401 \"no key set\" RCA — silent SecureKeyCache.save swallow)",
    "description": "Closes #1679\n### What changed\nProvider-key persistence failures are now loud at the moment they happen (gh-1679): the add/edit-provider wizard consumes the `SecureKeyCache.save` boolean it previously swallowed and prints a `/key set`-parity failure line (slot + store label + diagnostic, never the value); the recorded entry carries a persisted `keyNotPersisted` marker so the next boot prints one degradation line per affected slot with the retry command; the no-key skip reason / 401 hint renders a distinct \"secure store not writable\" state via `HostKeyResolver` (`storeDegraded`/`lastStoreError`) and `KeyStatusRenderer`; a missing macOS default keychain prints an advisory remedy (text only) and offers the repair as an explicit `[y/N]` step that re-attempts the save on `y`.\n\n### Key decisions\n- `SecureKeyCache` tracks failed-save NAMES with per-name diagnostics (success clears a name); the gh-1059 `saveFailures`/`lastSaveError` counters stay unchanged for `/key` status.\n- Cross-boot degradation rides the existing config persistence: a `keyNotPersisted: true` yaml field on `CustomProviderEntry` (absent when false — existing configs stay byte-identical); the boot note skips entries whose slot has since resolved.\n- Key resolution order untouched; golden gh-1570 / gh-1226 / gh-1000 fixtures pass unmodified. AC7's repair runs `security default-keychain -s …` only on an explicit `y`, through the injectable `ExecutionEnv`.\n- Second-tier items not in this card's core (env-provenance banner, pick-time masked prompt, `/key import-env`) were left out; wizard ⇄ `/key set` failure handling converges on the shared `could not save <slot> to <label>: the write failed` surface (locked by a parity test).\n\n### How to verify\n```bash\ndart test test/secrets/secure_key_save_degradation_test.dart \\\n  test/cli/provider_wizard_loud_save_test.dart \\\n  test/cli/secure_key_save_degradation_boot_test.dart \\\n  test/model_roles/provider_key_resolver_store_health_test.dart\ndart analyze lib bin\n```\n\n<details><summary>Architecture diagram</summary>\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  W[wizard key step] --> P[_persistSetupKey]\n  P -->|save true| E[entry + key, byte-identical]\n  P -->|save false| L[LOUD line: slot + label + diagnostic]\n  L --> D{missing default keychain?}\n  D -->|yes| O[\"[y/N] repair offer — runs only on y, then re-saves\"]\n  D -->|no| F[entry recorded with keyNotPersisted flag]\n  O -->|n| F\n  B[boot] --> N[secureKeySaveDegradationLines]\n  N -->|flagged entry, empty slot| BL[\"one line per slot + retry command (stderr)\"]\n  H[no-key hint / 401] --> S{store degraded?}\n  S -->|yes| HW[\"secure store not writable (diagnostic) … /key set\"]\n  S -->|no| HP[\"no key set; store one with /key set\"]\n```\n\n</details>"
  }
